    {
      "id": "t05",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 28,
      "y": 88,
      "width": 764,
      "height": 261.25,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "a6",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 3006,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 4006,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1770000000000,
      "link": "https://github.com/williamowen65/atlas-the-public-think-tank/blob/AppStartupAndWiring_visualization/src/Atlas.Console/Program.cs",
      "locked": false,
      "fontSize": 19,
      "fontFamily": 1,
      "text": "1. Resolve /data from AppContext.BaseDirectory.\n2. Build paths for nodes.json, node-types.json, documents.json, and participants.json.\n3. Create JsonNodeTypeRepository through INodeTypeRepository.\n4. Seed eight system types: Issue, Question, Idea, Solution, Evidence, Relationship, Comment, Location.\n5. Create JsonDocumentRepository and JsonParticipantRepository through boundary-owned interfaces.\n6. Find or create the “Legacy Console User” participant.\n7. Create JsonNodeRepository last because migration needs node types, documents, and a fallback author ID.\n8. Create the in-memory event publisher.\n9. Create the Content lifecycle observer and register its two handlers.\n10. Construct ConsoleApplication with repositories, event bus, file paths, and initial participant.\n11. Call application.Run(); startup ends and the interactive loop begins.",
      "rawText": "1. Resolve /data from AppContext.BaseDirectory.\n2. Build paths for nodes.json, node-types.json, documents.json, and participants.json.\n3. Create JsonNodeTypeRepository through INodeTypeRepository.\n4. Seed eight system types: Issue, Question, Idea, Solution, Evidence, Relationship, Comment, Location.\n5. Create JsonDocumentRepository and JsonParticipantRepository through boundary-owned interfaces.\n6. Find or create the “Legacy Console User” participant.\n7. Create JsonNodeRepository last because migration needs node types, documents, and a fallback author ID.\n8. Create the in-memory event publisher.\n9. Create the Content lifecycle observer and register its two handlers.\n10. Construct ConsoleApplication with repositories, event bus, file paths, and initial participant.\n11. Call application.Run(); startup ends and the interactive loop begins.",
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "1. Resolve /data from AppContext.BaseDirectory.\n2. Build paths for nodes.json, node-types.json, documents.json, and participants.json.\n3. Create JsonNodeTypeRepository through INodeTypeRepository.\n4. Seed eight system types: Issue, Question, Idea, Solution, Evidence, Relationship, Comment, Location.\n5. Create JsonDocumentRepository and JsonParticipantRepository through boundary-owned interfaces.\n6. Find or create the “Legacy Console User” participant.\n7. Create JsonNodeRepository last because migration needs node types, documents, and a fallback author ID.\n8. Create the in-memory event publisher.\n9. Create the Content lifecycle observer and register its two handlers.\n10. Construct ConsoleApplication with repositories, event bus, file paths, and initial participant.\n11. Call application.Run(); startup ends and the interactive loop begins.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
