      "versionNonce": 4012,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1770000000000,
      "link": "https://github.com/williamowen65/atlas-the-public-think-tank/blob/AppStartupAndWiring_visualization/src/Atlas.Console/Storage/JsonNodeRepository.cs",
      "locked": false,
      "fontSize": 19,
      "fontFamily": 1,
      "text": "SeedSystemNodeTypes runs before node repository construction.\n\nFor each required system type:\n• Match an existing type by case-insensitive name.\n• If found, enforce the current AutoPluralize setting and save it.\n• If missing, create a system-defined NodeTypeDefinition and save it.\n\nWhy order matters:\n• JsonNodeRepository may migrate legacy nodes during reads.\n• That migration resolves old type names and supplies Comment as the default requested sub-node type.\n• Therefore node types must already exist before node records are read/reconstituted.\n\nCurrent limitation:\n• Name uniqueness and this “required system types” policy are coordinated by the Console host.",
      "rawText": "SeedSystemNodeTypes runs before node repository construction.\n\nFor each required system type:\n• Match an existing type by case-insensitive name.\n• If found, enforce the current AutoPluralize setting and save it.\n• If missing, create a system-defined NodeTypeDefinition and save it.\n\nWhy order matters:\n• JsonNodeRepository may migrate legacy nodes during reads.\n• That migration resolves old type names and supplies Comment as the default requested sub-node type.\n• Therefore node types must already exist before node records are read/reconstituted.\n\nCurrent limitation:\n• Name uniqueness and this “required system types” policy are coordinated by the Console host.",
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "SeedSystemNodeTypes runs before node repository construction.\n\nFor each required system type:\n• Match an existing type by case-insensitive name.\n• If found, enforce the current AutoPluralize setting and save it.\n• If missing, create a system-defined NodeTypeDefinition and save it.\n\nWhy order matters:\n• JsonNodeRepository may migrate legacy nodes during reads.\n• That migration resolves old type names and supplies Comment as the default requested sub-node type.\n• Therefore node types must already exist before node records are read/reconstituted.\n\nCurrent limitation:\n• Name uniqueness and this “required system types” policy are coordinated by the Console host.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
