    },
    {
      "id": "t23",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 28,
      "y": 1673,
      "width": 764,
      "height": 356.25,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "a24",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 3024,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 4024,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1770000000000,
      "link": "https://github.com/williamowen65/atlas-the-public-think-tank/blob/AppStartupAndWiring_visualization/docs/architecture/CONTEXT-MAP.md",
      "locked": false,
      "fontSize": 19,
      "fontFamily": 1,
      "text": "Current prototype characteristics:\n• In-process and synchronous only.\n• Subscriber registrations disappear when the process exits.\n• No durable queue, outbox, retry, dead-letter handling, or idempotency support.\n• Publish does not isolate handler failures; an exception can interrupt dispatch.\n• Persistence across boundaries is not transactional.\n• JsonNodeRepository performs compatibility migration lazily when nodes are read.\n• Program.cs knows concrete adapters and startup order.\n\nLikely web-host translation:\n• Keep boundary-owned repository/application ports.\n• Replace manual Program.cs construction with web composition/DI.\n• Replace Console session participant with authenticated request identity.\n• Decide whether synchronous in-process notifications remain useful.\n• Design durable integration messaging separately if boundaries become independent services.",
      "rawText": "Current prototype characteristics:\n• In-process and synchronous only.\n• Subscriber registrations disappear when the process exits.\n• No durable queue, outbox, retry, dead-letter handling, or idempotency support.\n• Publish does not isolate handler failures; an exception can interrupt dispatch.\n• Persistence across boundaries is not transactional.\n• JsonNodeRepository performs compatibility migration lazily when nodes are read.\n• Program.cs knows concrete adapters and startup order.\n\nLikely web-host translation:\n• Keep boundary-owned repository/application ports.\n• Replace manual Program.cs construction with web composition/DI.\n• Replace Console session participant with authenticated request identity.\n• Decide whether synchronous in-process notifications remain useful.\n• Design durable integration messaging separately if boundaries become independent services.",
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Current prototype characteristics:\n• In-process and synchronous only.\n• Subscriber registrations disappear when the process exits.\n• No durable queue, outbox, retry, dead-letter handling, or idempotency support.\n• Publish does not isolate handler failures; an exception can interrupt dispatch.\n• Persistence across boundaries is not transactional.\n• JsonNodeRepository performs compatibility migration lazily when nodes are read.\n• Program.cs knows concrete adapters and startup order.\n\nLikely web-host translation:\n• Keep boundary-owned repository/application ports.\n• Replace manual Program.cs construction with web composition/DI.\n• Replace Console session participant with authenticated request identity.\n• Decide whether synchronous in-process notifications remain useful.\n• Design durable integration messaging separately if boundaries become independent services.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
